From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:29:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: NT change notify delivery, PathMakeUniqueName,
 temporary item properties, view state (3258)

- NTSHChangeNotifyRegister registers with the new delivery (the window
  gets a shared block that SHChangeNotification_Lock reads), as the
  function is documented; NTSHChangeNotifyDeregister already matched.
- PathMakeUniqueName makes "<long template> (n)" (n from 1) in the
  directory, or the short template with the number for 8.3 volumes; it
  returned TRUE and left the buffer alone. The A form converts.
- IKnownFolder::GetRedirectionCapabilities answers 0 for a fixed folder
  (the Wine test's todo_wine removed), DENY_ALL for others as before.
- SHSetTemporaryPropertyForItem keeps the value in a store of the item;
  new SHGetTemporaryPropertyForItem and IShellItem2::GetPropertyStore
  (GPS_TEMPORARY) read it back. shell32 delay-imports propsys.
- IShellImageData::SetEncoderParams keeps the property bag (always S_OK).
- IShellView: AddPropertySheetPages succeeds (the view has no pages),
  GetView returns the VID of the current mode (E_INVALIDARG for another
  type), SaveViewState writes the view mode into the browser's view
  state stream (also when the view window is destroyed) and the next
  view reads it back.

